<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds were firm in late trade on Monday, sustained by gains on other markets amid few fresh domestic factors, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We've got a few quiet days ahead of us, with no major indicators due and with a likely focus abroad, especially for the longer end of the market. But the underlying tone is still good,&quot; said Juan Antonio Mielgo, economist at Bank of America in Madrid.</p>
<p>He said attention will probably turn to June inflation data due at the end of the week, though the possibility of the figure moving the market was limited.</p>
</text>
